{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `e060666f`: the conservative stop. E4 gets no projection\nadapter.\n\n1. An `also.via` selector that passes through the reference of a\n   pending source has no recorded row yet. E4 stops that submit\n   before retention and before any signing. It writes nothing.\n2. The stop has one name, and the E4 note states it. Use the present\n   stop for an unresolved source if the client has one. If it has\n   none, propose a name with the source.\n3. When the row is recorded, the same submit goes through the\n   ordinary checked path. E4 adds no second evaluator, guesses no\n   reference and calls no test seam.\n4. The direct route stays in E4 with its witness: a batch whose step\n   names an `output` or an `after` source, the fill from the real\n   source entry, and the signing of that same retained position.\n5. Step E5 owns the selection through a pending source, by a checked\n   hypothetical view. Section 13 gives E5 the materialized act and\n   the waits. I add this case to the E5 request `b1c6aad6` when E5\n   starts.\n\nOne case in E4 shows the stop and shows that both stores are\nunchanged after it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}